{# Contextual "here is the tool for this" box inside an article.
   Driven by one line of front matter: `toolCta: knees`.

   Why it exists: on Aug 13, 2026 only the threshold article linked a tool. The
   marathon, durability, volume and cycling articles all ranked, took traffic,
   and pointed at nothing in the members library — the cheapest distribution the
   business owns, entirely unused.

   Where it links matters as much as that it links. Gated tools point at the
   All-Access library anchor, NOT at the tool: sending a public reader to a login
   wall converts nothing and reads as a bait. The zones calculator has a real
   public version, so that one goes straight to the tool. Both destinations, and
   the wording, come from site/_data/library.json — the same file the sales pages
   render from, so a URL change lands everywhere at once. #}
{%- if toolCta %}
{%- set lib = library[lang] or library.es -%}
{%- for item in lib.live -%}
{%- if item.key == toolCta %}
<aside class="tool-cta">
  <span class="tool-cta-label">{{ lib.ctaLabel }}{% if item.gated %} · {{ lib.ctaGated }}{% endif %}</span>
  <h3>{{ item.name }}</h3>
  <p>{{ item.desc }}</p>
  <a href="{{ item.url }}">{% if item.gated %}{{ lib.ctaSee }}{% else %}{{ lib.ctaOpen }}{% endif %}</a>
</aside>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
